#EXP-1785: the HEADER's trailing slot starts with THE waiting chips again (wide: one StripChip per waiting plan/question of the tree; phones: ONE button + count opening THE Menu), waiting-cards.json owns them. #EXP-1732 (EDE-63, owner 2026-11-07; drafts c13140f9 session, ff3f91ca agent, de58c149 app) THE SESSION SCREEN ×4: ONE screen for a chat (a root session), a team agent's conversation, the Assistant's and an app's editor session (an app IS its agent's session); the list and the sidebar entry stay `Chats` (chats.json). AMENDS session-chat.json (the strip: `+`, Conversation, issue/session chips, the group tab, the plan tab, the pinned Results tab are GONE ×4; the chip strip is deleted, not hidden), chats.json `agentChat.tabs/planTabs/pageCases` (an agent's chat gets the same tabs) and apps.json THE EDITOR's `editorTabs` (wide/phone/menu tab sets: the app gets this screen's tabs; Versions is a tab, Settings is a `…` entry). HEADER (every width, every kind): the lead avatar (a chat: THE ChatHeaderTitle lead disc; an agent: its disc, the Assistant: THE brand mark; an app: its BoardGlyph + the version pill), the title (one truncated line) over ONE subtitle line `subtitle({status, device, trigger})` = the non-blank parts joined by `copy.separator` (status = the session's state word, device = its device's name, trigger = an agent's first enabled trigger's `triggerSummary`, else null); then the trailing slot: the merge status pill (merge-train.json, while `guidePullRequest`), an app's Publish (apps.json), the `…` (THE session screen menu, `sessionScreenMenu`, testId `testIds.menu`; #FEED-239: there is NO gear any more ×4). #EXP-1762 (Danny, ONE header line): on WIDE (web ≥ md, the IDE) the tabs sit ON the header row, after the title/subtitle block and before the trailing slot; on PHONES (web-mobile too) under the header row: ONE SegmentedControl (THE existing one ×4 + Exponential UI, no new component), testId `testIds.tabs`, its options = `tabs` in order, each the label `copy.tabs[id]` followed by its `count` as a muted number when not null; on a phone it scrolls sideways when it overflows (never icon-only, never wrapping). TABS BY KIND (`kinds`): a chat, an agent and the Assistant = chat · issues · sessions · results; an app = chat · preview · data · versions (#FEED-239: an app has no Sessions or Results tab; a requested one falls back to the default). COUNTS (`count`, issues/sessions/results only; 0 = null): issues = every issue of the tree (session-chat.json's union, nested ones included), sessions = every session UNDER the root (its children and theirs; #EXP-1731's subagent children included; the root itself never), results = results-tab.json's results of the tree. SETTINGS (`settings`): agent, assistant and app; never a chat. The `…`'s settings entry (`copy.menu.settings[kind]`, concept `nav-settings`) opens the kind's SETTINGS as an opened item (`open: settings`), the same pane on every path (#FEED-239: never a navigation to the Settings screen; a sidebar row's `…` › settings opens that chat with `open: settings`): an agent = THE agent settings page body (agent-settings.json: prompt, triggers, defaults; the Assistant's = settings/assistant), an app = the app's settings page (apps.json Settings; Export and Delete are NOT on it, they are `…` entries). BODIES: chat = the ROOT's OWN SESSION VIEW for EVERY kind (owner 2026-11-08): its raw work (THE ONE transcript of #EXP-1736 transcript-grouping.json: MessageBubble + avatar + name, the tool/thought/subagent `trace` rows under the agent's bubble) with its own message cards inline, THE Dock and THE composer (the view NEW-46 showed on a single-session chat, now always; the old dispatcher Conversation without the root's work is gone; no second message view anywhere); no session's work is visible nowhere: the root's = Chat, every descendant's = its Sessions row, a single-session chat's Sessions tab is empty (never a row for the root itself); plans and questions stay INLINE in it (and in Needs you); a plan row opens the plan page (plan-page.json) as an opened item. issues = the tree's issues as THE issue rows (status glyph, mono identifier, title; nested ones indented under their parent), (#EXP-1834: no `+` over it any more: linking is the `…`'s `linkIssue` entry); a row opens that issue IN PLACE (`open: issue`, the embedded issue body of session-chat.json EXP-1316). sessions = THE tree rows of every session under the root (SessionRow small + TreeGuides, markState, subagents included as child rows); a row opens that session IN PLACE (`open: session`, the raw work + its composer). results = results-tab.json's body. preview / data / versions = apps.json's Preview, Data (app-records.json `dataTab`) and Versions bodies. An OPENED item (issue, session, plan, settings): WIDE = no back link (#FEED-239, owner 2026-11-13): the right pane (a tab's body or the opened item) leads with THE collapse button (`collapse` true; the existing ghost icon button, concept `ui-pane-collapse`, label `copy.collapse`, testId `testIds.collapse`, right-aligned in a slim row) that closes the right pane = `?tab=chat` and no item (the chat full width; an app's strip then shows no selected segment); pressing ANY tab, the active one too, closes the opened item and shows that tab; PHONES = the pushed page's `‹` header back to the tab it came from (settings and a plan: back to where they were opened). LAYOUT (`sessionScreen`, every mirror replays `cases` comparing the WHOLE value): WIDE (web ≥ `beside.breakpoint` px and the IDE) = the beside rule: whenever the active tab is not chat OR an item is opened, the body = TWO panes, the chat pane (`beside.chat` fr, min `beside.chatMinWidth` px, THE same chat body with its composer) : the tab pane (`beside.pane` fr, the active tab's body, or the opened item over it), a hairline between (`layout: beside`, testId `testIds.beside`); the Chat tab alone = the chat full width (`layout: chat`). NARROW (phones, web < breakpoint) = ONE pane: `chat`, the tab's body (`tab`) or the opened item (`item`, a pushed page over the tab). ACTIVE = the requested tab when it is one of the kind's tabs (legacy `?tab=` values map through `legacyTabs` first), else the kind's default: an app `preview` when wide (apps.json), else `chat`. OPEN (`open` in: issue | session | plan | settings, anything else = null): a requested `settings` (the retired app `?tab=settings`) opens settings when nothing else is open; settings only with `settings` (else null). ALGORITHM: k = `kinds[kind]` (unknown = session); tabs = k.tabs as {id, label, count, disabled (counted and count = 0)}, minus `chat` when wide and not k.wideChatTab (#FEED-239: an app's chat is the pinned left pane on wide, so its strip is Preview · Data · Versions; phones keep Chat); req = `legacyTabs[requested]` ?? requested; active = req when in k.tabs and not an empty counted tab, else (wide ? k.wideDefault : `chat`); layout = wide ? (active ≠ chat or open ? `beside` : `chat`) : (open ? `item` : active = chat ? `chat` : `tab`); collapse = layout = `beside`. Mirrors: TS src/session-screen.ts, desktop `domain::session_screen`, iOS ExpCore `SessionScreen.swift`, Android `domain/SessionScreen.kt`. STATUS WORD (owner 2026-11-09, one rule ×4, `sessionScreenStatus`, every mirror replays `statusCases`): the subtitle's `status` = THE TREE's word, lowercase `copy.status`: `needsInput` while any non-ended session of the tree needs input, else `working` while any non-ended one is busy, else `queued` while the root is queued, else `done` once the root ended, else `idle` (an empty tree = `idle`); it is never dropped. An app's subtitle = this word · apps.json `editorHeader`'s DEVICE part (the device's name, else `copy.noDeviceOnline`) and that function's TONE; a chat's and an agent's device = the root's device name. ACTIVE FOLLOWS THE OPENED ITEM: `open` session = the `sessions` tab active, `open` issue = `issues`, when the kind has that tab (a plan and settings keep the active tab). TAB SIZING ×4: every segment is sized to its label (+ count), never stretched to equal widths and never squeezed; the strip scrolls sideways when it overflows. APP LEAD ×4: the app's BoardGlyph sits IN the lead disc (the chat header's `disc` on the muted fill), never bare, the version pill right after the name. PHONE ITEM ×4 (web-mobile too): an opened item is a pushed page: its own header (‹ back + the item's title) replaces the screen header AND the tabs. TONE ×4: the subtitle wears editorHeader's tones: `attention` (the needs-input amber) while the word is needsInput (an app also while its device part is `copy.noDeviceOnline`), `active` while working or queued, else `muted`.",
